5:T417,"Moh Phaans Jaga Bandhi Rahyao, Bishthure Kaam Bilaap.
Bichure Kaam Bilaap, Maani Sut, Pitu, Pati, Maata.
Sasur, Jamaee, Jubati, Suhrid, Guru, Sish, Dhan, Bhraata.
Nij Anubhav Ki Bhool, Bihaar Bhagavat Biramaye.
Ko Ham, Kahaan Ko Jaata, Kahaan Te, Kihi Lagi Aaye."
- Shri Bhagwat Rasik, Bhagwat Rasik Ki Vani, AnanyaNishchayatma Granth - Uttarardh (34)
The living beings neither have come with anyone in this world and nor have gone with anyone. (All are born alone and die alone). All these companions made in this world in the course of the time only. The world is trapped in false attachments, so people mourn for father, son, mother, father-in-law, son in law, wife, friend, master, disciple, wealth, brothers etc. as they believe they all are their own. Bhagvat Rasik ji says that, due to lack of experience, people have been lost in the false, temporary happiness of the world so that they have gone unaware of the ultimate truth of human life that, Who we are, where we are going, where we are coming from, for which reason we come for etc.7:["slug","shri-bhagavat-rasik-bhagavat-rasik-ki-vani-ananyanishchayatm-granth-uttarardh-34","d"]
